        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'When does the Lindsay Clancy trial start?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'It is underway. Jury selection ran July 20 to July 23, 2026, in Plymouth County Superior Court before Judge William F. Sullivan, and an 18-juror panel was seated — 12 jurors and 6 alternates. Opening statements were delivered on Monday, July 27, 2026, and the children’s father, Patrick Clancy, testified as the first witness. The judge has said the trial could run several weeks and potentially up to two months. Prosecutors dropped three duplicative strangulation counts on July 9, leaving three counts of first-degree murder. She has pleaded not guilty and is presumed innocent.' } },
