---
<Base
  title="True Crime Court Calendar: Trial Dates & Hearings 2026"
  description="Track verified 2026 true-crime trial dates, hearings, sentencing proceedings, and appeals, including the Tupac Shakur murder trial, Lindsay Clancy, and other major cases."
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Court Calendar</p>
    <h1>True Crime Court Calendar: Trial Dates &amp; Hearings 2026</h1>
    <p class="cal-answer">
      Duane &ldquo;Keffe D&rdquo; Davis&rsquo;s trial in the Tupac Shakur murder case is scheduled to begin with jury selection on <strong>Monday, August 10</strong> in Las Vegas. Colt Gray pleaded guilty <strong>July 24</strong> to all 55 counts in the Apalachee High School shooting; his sentencing hearing resumed <strong>Monday, July 27</strong> in Barrow County and no sentence has been imposed yet, and his father Colin Gray is sentenced <strong>July 30</strong>. Opening statements in Lindsay Clancy&rsquo;s murder trial were delivered <strong>Monday, July 27</strong> in Plymouth County. David Anthony Burke, known as D4vd, was held to answer on all charges on <strong>July 27</strong> at the close of a five-day preliminary hearing in Los Angeles and is due back for arraignment <strong>August 31</strong>. Karmelo Anthony has his first post-conviction hearings <strong>August 19 and 20</strong> in Collin County, Texas. Dianne Curry Peck&rsquo;s pretrial conference is set for <strong>August 31</strong> in Fall River, Yvonne &ldquo;Missy&rdquo; Woods is sentenced <strong>September 8</strong> in Jefferson County, Colorado, and Larry Millete is sentenced <strong>September 29</strong> in Chula Vista.
    </p>
    <p class="cal-fresh">
      <strong>Last full sweep: {LAST_VERIFIED}.</strong> Court dates move. Every entry below is checked against the public record, carries its source, and carries the date <em>that entry</em> was last verified &mdash; we do not re-date a card nobody re-checked. Confirm with the court before you travel.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="about-this-calendar">
    <h2 id="about-this-calendar" class="cal-notice__h">About this calendar</h2>
    <div class="cal-notice">
      <p>
        <strong>About this calendar:</strong> Neural Edge Publishing provides this calendar as a best-effort informational resource for readers following publicly reported court proceedings and case developments. Inclusion does not imply endorsement, guilt, credibility, or editorial approval. Allegations, arrests, and charges are not convictions. Court dates, legal status, and other information may change. Each entry identifies the sources and date used for its latest review. Readers should consult the linked court or government source for the most current official information and may report a correction through the correction link provided.
      </p>
      <p class="cal-notice__links">
        <a href="/court-calendar-policy/">Read the full Court Calendar and Case-Tracking Policy</a>
        <a href={CORRECTION_MAILTO}>Report a correction</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="next-dates">
    <h2 id="next-dates">Next Court Dates</h2>
    <p class="cal-sub">Everything currently on a calendar, in date order.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      {nextDates.map((e) => (
        <article class="card" id={e.id}>
          <p class="card__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
          <h3 class="card__case">{e.case}</h3>
          <p class="card__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time></p>
          <p class="card__court">{e.court}</p>
          {e.docket && <p class="card__docket">{e.docket}</p>}
          <p class="card__status"><span class="card__k">Status</span> {e.status}</p>
          <p class="card__detail">{e.detail}</p>
          {e.nextNote && <p class="card__nodate"><span class="card__k">Next court date</span> {e.nextNote}</p>}
          <p class="card__meta">
            <span class="card__verified">Last verified: {e.verified || LAST_VERIFIED}</span>
            <span class="card__change">All dates are subject to change by the court.</span>
          </p>
          <p class="card__src">
            <span class="card__k">Source</span>
            <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a>
            <span class="card__srctype">{e.srcType}</span>
            {e.src2 && <a class="card__src2" href={e.src2} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel2}</a>}
          </p>
          <p class="card__links">
            {e.link ? (
              <a class="card__read" href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a>
            ) : (
              <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>
            )}
            {e.link2 && <a class="card__read" href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>}
            <a class="card__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a>
            <a class="card__help" href={CORRECTION_MAILTO}>Report a correction</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec">
    <div class="capture-cta" aria-label="Stay current on this court calendar and get the free case-reading guide">
      <p class="capture-cta__eyebrow">Came here for a date?</p>
      <h2 class="capture-cta__head">We&rsquo;ll keep you current on the calendar.</h2>
      <p class="capture-cta__body">
        Court dates move &mdash; and so does what a hearing actually settles. We&rsquo;ll send you <em>How to Read a Case Like the Court Does</em> &mdash; a plain-language framework for weighing evidence instead of guessing, and what a verdict really settles (and what it doesn&rsquo;t) &mdash; plus calendar updates when dates change. No weekly blast; unsubscribe anytime.
      </p>
      <a class="capture-cta__btn" href="https://cassiancreed.beehiiv.com/subscribe?utm_source=website&utm_medium=court_calendar&utm_campaign=lm_case_how-to-read-a-case">
        Get the guide &amp; date updates
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="upcoming-trials">
    <h2 id="upcoming-trials">Upcoming Trials</h2>
    {byGroup('trials').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        {e.docket && <p class="row__docket">{e.docket}</p>}
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        {e.nextNote && <p class="row__nodate"><strong>Next court date:</strong> {e.nextNote}</p>}
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {e.verified || LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} {e.link2 && <a href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a> <a class="row__help" href={CORRECTION_MAILTO}>Report a correction</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="hearings">
    <h2 id="hearings">Hearings &amp; Pretrial</h2>
    {byGroup('hearings').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        {e.docket && <p class="row__docket">{e.docket}</p>}
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        {e.nextNote && <p class="row__nodate"><strong>Next court date:</strong> {e.nextNote}</p>}
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {e.verified || LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">
          {e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>}
          <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a> <a class="row__help" href={CORRECTION_MAILTO}>Report a correction</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="sentencing">
    <h2 id="sentencing">Sentencing &amp; Appeals</h2>
    {byGroup('sentencing').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        {e.docket && <p class="row__docket">{e.docket}</p>}
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        {e.nextNote && <p class="row__nodate"><strong>Next court date:</strong> {e.nextNote}</p>}
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {e.verified || LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} {e.link2 && <a href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a> <a class="row__help" href={CORRECTION_MAILTO}>Report a correction</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
    {appeals.map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.type || 'Post-conviction motions'}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when">{e.where}</p>
        <p class="row__nodate"><strong>Next court date:</strong> {NO_DATE}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        {e.nextNote && <p class="row__nodate"><strong>Next court date:</strong> {e.nextNote}</p>}
        <p class="row__note">{e.note}</p>
